1
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:13,080
August 1590

2
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:15,160
An English ship drops anchor off the coast of

3
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:16,310
North America

4
00:00:16,460 --> 00:00:18,090
On board is a man who has waited three

5
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:19,730
years to come back to his daughter and his

6
00:00:19,730 --> 00:00:20,998
baby granddaughter

7
00:00:21,148 --> 00:00:22,218
His name is John White,

8
00:00:22,218 --> 00:00:24,058
and he is the governor of this tiny English

9
00:00:24,058 --> 00:00:24,959
colony

10
00:00:25,109 --> 00:00:26,459
But when he reaches the settlement,

11
00:00:26,459 --> 00:00:27,179
it is empty

12
00:00:27,179 --> 00:00:29,530
More than one hundred people have vanished

13
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:31,230
The only clue is a single word,

14
00:00:31,230 --> 00:00:33,127
carved into a wooden post

15
00:00:33,277 --> 00:00:34,467
Four hundred years later,

16
00:00:34,467 --> 00:00:36,625
we still don't know what it means

17
00:00:36,775 --> 00:00:38,706
This is the mystery of the Lost Colony of

18
00:00:38,706 --> 00:00:39,826
Roanoke

19
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:45,000
In the 1580s,

20
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,600
England was racing Spain to build an empire in

21
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:49,040
the Americas

22
00:00:49,273 --> 00:00:51,303
Spain had already grown rich from gold and

23
00:00:51,303 --> 00:00:53,280
silver in the Americas

24
00:00:53,430 --> 00:00:55,420
Queen Elizabeth gave an explorer named Sir

25
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:58,020
Walter Raleigh permission to start a colony

26
00:00:58,388 --> 00:00:59,058
A year earlier,

27
00:00:59,058 --> 00:01:01,178
his explorers had come back with stories of a

28
00:01:01,178 --> 00:01:01,458
rich,

29
00:01:01,458 --> 00:01:02,218
green land,

30
00:01:02,218 --> 00:01:03,638
and two local men,

31
00:01:03,638 --> 00:01:05,398
Manteo and Wanchese

32
00:01:05,773 --> 00:01:07,803
In 1585,

33
00:01:07,803 --> 00:01:09,883
his first group of men landed on Roanoke

34
00:01:09,883 --> 00:01:10,283
Island,

35
00:01:10,283 --> 00:01:12,624
in what is now North Carolina

36
00:01:12,774 --> 00:01:14,004
John White came too,

37
00:01:14,004 --> 00:01:14,804
as an artist,

38
00:01:14,804 --> 00:01:15,844
painting the people,

39
00:01:15,844 --> 00:01:17,977
plants and animals he saw

40
00:01:18,127 --> 00:01:19,197
They ran short of food,

41
00:01:19,197 --> 00:01:21,577
and quarreled with the local people

42
00:01:21,727 --> 00:01:22,637
Fighting broke out,

43
00:01:22,637 --> 00:01:24,797
and trust between the English and some of the

44
00:01:24,797 --> 00:01:26,860
local people was broken

45
00:01:27,010 --> 00:01:27,820
But one man,

46
00:01:27,820 --> 00:01:28,280
Manteo,

47
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:29,520
from Croatoan island,

48
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:31,922
stayed a loyal friend to the English

49
00:01:32,072 --> 00:01:33,102
After less than a year,

50
00:01:33,102 --> 00:01:34,462
they gave up and sailed home

51
00:01:34,462 --> 00:01:37,018
But Raleigh wanted to try again

52
00:01:37,168 --> 00:01:37,678
This time,

53
00:01:37,678 --> 00:01:39,758
he would send families

54
00:01:43,283 --> 00:01:45,313
In 1587,

55
00:01:45,313 --> 00:01:46,833
a new group set sail

56
00:01:46,833 --> 00:01:47,353
This time,

57
00:01:47,353 --> 00:01:49,426
it was not just soldiers

58
00:01:49,576 --> 00:01:50,206
There were farmers,

59
00:01:50,206 --> 00:01:51,686
craftsmen and whole families,

60
00:01:51,686 --> 00:01:54,286
including women who were expecting babies

61
00:01:54,697 --> 00:01:56,647
About one hundred and fifteen men,

62
00:01:56,647 --> 00:01:59,247
women and children came to build a real town

63
00:02:00,084 --> 00:02:02,354
Each family was promised a large piece of land

64
00:02:02,354 --> 00:02:03,824
in the new world

65
00:02:03,974 --> 00:02:05,044
Their leader was John White,

66
00:02:05,044 --> 00:02:07,044
an artist who had painted the land and its

67
00:02:07,044 --> 00:02:08,701
people on the first trip

68
00:02:08,851 --> 00:02:10,081
Manteo sailed with them,

69
00:02:10,081 --> 00:02:12,544
coming home after a trip to England

70
00:02:12,694 --> 00:02:14,324
They were supposed to settle further north,

71
00:02:14,324 --> 00:02:16,084
near Chesapeake Bay

72
00:02:16,271 --> 00:02:16,701
On the way,

73
00:02:16,701 --> 00:02:17,901
they stopped at Roanoke,

74
00:02:17,901 --> 00:02:19,421
to check on a few men left there the

75
00:02:19,421 --> 00:02:20,696
year before

76
00:02:20,846 --> 00:02:22,636
But the ship's captain refused to take them

77
00:02:22,636 --> 00:02:22,956
further,

78
00:02:22,956 --> 00:02:24,476
and left them on Roanoke Island,

79
00:02:24,476 --> 00:02:26,175
late in the summer

80
00:02:26,325 --> 00:02:27,835
They found the old fort torn down,

81
00:02:27,835 --> 00:02:30,435
and the empty houses overgrown with weeds

82
00:02:34,617 --> 00:02:35,767
On August 18th,

83
00:02:35,767 --> 00:02:38,007
John White's daughter Eleanor gave birth to a

84
00:02:38,007 --> 00:02:39,309
baby girl

85
00:02:39,459 --> 00:02:40,129
Her husband,

86
00:02:40,129 --> 00:02:41,009
Ananias Dare,

87
00:02:41,009 --> 00:02:42,990
was one of the colonists

88
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:44,170
They named her Virginia

89
00:02:44,170 --> 00:02:46,210
She was the first English child born in the

90
00:02:46,210 --> 00:02:47,330
Americas

91
00:02:47,715 --> 00:02:48,385
Days later,

92
00:02:48,385 --> 00:02:50,932
another baby was born in the colony

93
00:02:51,082 --> 00:02:52,312
But the colony was in trouble

94
00:02:52,312 --> 00:02:53,992
It was too late in the year to plant

95
00:02:53,992 --> 00:02:55,112
crops

96
00:02:55,285 --> 00:02:57,195
The supplies they had brought from England were

97
00:02:57,195 --> 00:02:58,955
already running low

98
00:02:59,147 --> 00:03:00,947
Relations with some of the local people were

99
00:03:00,947 --> 00:03:02,010
tense

100
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:03,870
Manteo was baptized as a Christian,

101
00:03:03,870 --> 00:03:06,470
and named Lord of Roanoke by the English

102
00:03:06,793 --> 00:03:09,262
So the colonists asked John White to sail back

103
00:03:09,262 --> 00:03:09,862
to England,

104
00:03:09,862 --> 00:03:11,376
and bring help

105
00:03:11,526 --> 00:03:12,516
White was their governor,

106
00:03:12,516 --> 00:03:13,676
and leaving felt wrong

107
00:03:13,676 --> 00:03:15,756
But the colonists insisted

108
00:03:19,383 --> 00:03:21,983
White did not want to leave his family behind

109
00:03:22,391 --> 00:03:22,901
His daughter,

110
00:03:22,901 --> 00:03:25,501
and a granddaughter only nine days old

111
00:03:25,700 --> 00:03:26,530
Before he went,

112
00:03:26,530 --> 00:03:28,906
they agreed on a simple signal

113
00:03:29,056 --> 00:03:30,966
The colonists were already planning to move

114
00:03:30,966 --> 00:03:32,958
about fifty miles inland

115
00:03:33,108 --> 00:03:34,378
If the colonists moved,

116
00:03:34,378 --> 00:03:36,098
they would carve the name of the place they

117
00:03:36,098 --> 00:03:36,658
had gone,

118
00:03:36,658 --> 00:03:38,590
on a tree or post

119
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:39,329
That way,

120
00:03:39,329 --> 00:03:41,929
anyone coming back would know where to look

121
00:03:42,165 --> 00:03:43,235
And if they were in danger,

122
00:03:43,235 --> 00:03:45,440
they would carve a cross above it

123
00:03:45,590 --> 00:03:46,500
A cross would mean:

124
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:47,260
come quickly,

125
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:48,727
we need help

126
00:03:48,877 --> 00:03:50,587
White promised to return within months

127
00:03:50,587 --> 00:03:51,387
He sailed away,

128
00:03:51,387 --> 00:03:53,987
and left his daughter and granddaughter behind

129
00:03:54,379 --> 00:03:55,929
Nobody knew it would be the last time he

130
00:03:55,929 --> 00:03:57,369
saw them

131
00:04:00,717 --> 00:04:01,907
When White reached England,

132
00:04:01,907 --> 00:04:04,306
the country was preparing for war

133
00:04:04,456 --> 00:04:07,046
Spain's King Philip had built a giant fleet to

134
00:04:07,046 --> 00:04:08,486
conquer England

135
00:04:08,741 --> 00:04:10,011
A huge Spanish fleet,

136
00:04:10,011 --> 00:04:10,851
the Armada,

137
00:04:10,851 --> 00:04:12,736
was coming to invade

138
00:04:12,886 --> 00:04:15,356
In the summer of 1588,

139
00:04:15,356 --> 00:04:17,476
English ships fought the Armada in the English

140
00:04:17,476 --> 00:04:18,495
Channel

141
00:04:18,645 --> 00:04:20,195
The Queen needed every ship she had

142
00:04:20,195 --> 00:04:22,721
No ships could be spared for the colony

143
00:04:22,871 --> 00:04:23,741
White begged for help,

144
00:04:23,741 --> 00:04:25,861
but a few colonists far away were not the

145
00:04:25,861 --> 00:04:27,621
Queen's first concern

146
00:04:27,829 --> 00:04:29,539
White did find two small ships,

147
00:04:29,539 --> 00:04:31,499
but they were attacked at sea and forced to

148
00:04:31,499 --> 00:04:32,730
turn back

149
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:34,710
French pirates robbed them of almost

150
00:04:34,710 --> 00:04:35,830
everything

151
00:04:36,074 --> 00:04:37,264
Months turned into years

152
00:04:37,264 --> 00:04:39,384
It would be three years before he saw Roanoke

153
00:04:39,384 --> 00:04:40,504
again

154
00:04:40,659 --> 00:04:42,369
In 1590,

155
00:04:42,369 --> 00:04:44,809
he finally found a place on ships sailing out

156
00:04:44,809 --> 00:04:47,209
to hunt for Spanish treasure

157
00:04:50,317 --> 00:04:53,840
White finally landed on Roanoke on August 18th,

158
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:54,747
1590

159
00:04:54,747 --> 00:04:57,250
It was his granddaughter's third birthday

160
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,030
From the ship,

161
00:04:58,030 --> 00:05:00,070
they saw smoke rising on the island,

162
00:05:00,070 --> 00:05:02,242
and hoped it was the colonists

163
00:05:02,392 --> 00:05:03,422
As they came close,

164
00:05:03,422 --> 00:05:05,782
his men blew a trumpet and sang English songs

165
00:05:05,782 --> 00:05:07,222
Nobody answered

166
00:05:07,490 --> 00:05:09,040
They waited near the shore through the night,

167
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:11,640
and at dawn walked to the village

168
00:05:11,821 --> 00:05:13,251
The houses had been taken down,

169
00:05:13,251 --> 00:05:15,851
and a tall wooden fence stood around the site

170
00:05:16,303 --> 00:05:18,573
Heavy things like iron bars and lead had been

171
00:05:18,573 --> 00:05:19,373
left behind,

172
00:05:19,373 --> 00:05:21,453
now covered in grass

173
00:05:21,621 --> 00:05:22,451
There were no graves,

174
00:05:22,451 --> 00:05:24,455
and no sign of a battle

175
00:05:24,605 --> 00:05:25,995
White found his own chests,

176
00:05:25,995 --> 00:05:27,395
dug up and broken open

177
00:05:27,395 --> 00:05:28,115
His books,

178
00:05:28,115 --> 00:05:30,715
maps and pictures were ruined by the rain

179
00:05:31,084 --> 00:05:32,844
Everyone was gone

180
00:05:33,033 --> 00:05:34,743
More than one hundred people had simply

181
00:05:34,743 --> 00:05:35,863
disappeared

182
00:05:39,650 --> 00:05:40,240
Then they found it

183
00:05:40,240 --> 00:05:41,440
On a post of the fence,

184
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:42,880
someone had carved one word:

185
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:44,000
CROATOAN

186
00:05:44,596 --> 00:05:45,666
The bark had been removed,

187
00:05:45,666 --> 00:05:47,146
and the letters were cut neatly,

188
00:05:47,146 --> 00:05:48,906
in large capitals

189
00:05:49,067 --> 00:05:51,337
On a nearby tree were three more letters:

190
00:05:51,337 --> 00:05:51,577
C,

191
00:05:51,577 --> 00:05:52,057
R,

192
00:05:52,057 --> 00:05:53,177
O

193
00:05:53,351 --> 00:05:55,221
These were the signs the colonists had promised

194
00:05:55,221 --> 00:05:56,325
to leave

195
00:05:56,475 --> 00:05:57,505
And there was no cross

196
00:05:57,505 --> 00:05:59,541
No sign of danger

197
00:05:59,691 --> 00:06:01,361
It looked as if they had left calmly,

198
00:06:01,361 --> 00:06:02,804
and in peace

199
00:06:02,954 --> 00:06:05,824
Croatoan was the name of an island about fifty

200
00:06:05,824 --> 00:06:06,824
miles south,

201
00:06:06,824 --> 00:06:08,904
home to friendly people

202
00:06:09,108 --> 00:06:10,658
It was also the home of Manteo,

203
00:06:10,658 --> 00:06:12,738
the colonists' loyal friend

204
00:06:13,149 --> 00:06:15,749
White was sure his family had gone there

205
00:06:16,051 --> 00:06:16,401
Help,

206
00:06:16,401 --> 00:06:17,041
it seemed,

207
00:06:17,041 --> 00:06:19,641
was only one short voyage away

208
00:06:23,117 --> 00:06:25,717
White wanted to sail to Croatoan straight away

209
00:06:26,403 --> 00:06:27,513
They rowed back to the ships,

210
00:06:27,513 --> 00:06:29,319
ready to sail south

211
00:06:29,469 --> 00:06:30,579
But a violent storm hit

212
00:06:30,579 --> 00:06:31,939
The ship lost its anchors,

213
00:06:31,939 --> 00:06:33,627
and was nearly wrecked

214
00:06:33,807 --> 00:06:34,407
Ropes snapped,

215
00:06:34,407 --> 00:06:35,807
the sailors were exhausted,

216
00:06:35,807 --> 00:06:38,407
and food and fresh water were running low

217
00:06:38,804 --> 00:06:40,114
They planned to spend the winter in the

218
00:06:40,114 --> 00:06:40,714
Caribbean,

219
00:06:40,714 --> 00:06:42,718
and come back in the spring

220
00:06:42,868 --> 00:06:44,898
But strong winds kept pushing them east,

221
00:06:44,898 --> 00:06:46,573
across the ocean

222
00:06:46,723 --> 00:06:49,323
The captain decided to turn back to England

223
00:06:49,568 --> 00:06:51,973
John White never returned to America

224
00:06:52,123 --> 00:06:53,793
He later wrote that he could only leave them

225
00:06:53,793 --> 00:06:55,433
in God's hands

226
00:06:55,583 --> 00:06:57,213
He never found out what happened to his

227
00:06:57,213 --> 00:06:57,573
daughter,

228
00:06:57,573 --> 00:06:59,333
or his granddaughter

229
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:04,940
The simplest theory is that the colonists did

230
00:07:04,940 --> 00:07:05,940
what the carving said,

231
00:07:05,940 --> 00:07:08,324
and moved to Croatoan island

232
00:07:08,474 --> 00:07:10,184
Croatoan was Manteo's home,

233
00:07:10,184 --> 00:07:12,784
and his people were friendly to the English

234
00:07:12,945 --> 00:07:13,335
Today,

235
00:07:13,335 --> 00:07:15,698
that island is called Hatteras

236
00:07:15,848 --> 00:07:16,518
It is a long,

237
00:07:16,518 --> 00:07:18,238
thin island in the Outer Banks,

238
00:07:18,238 --> 00:07:20,737
about fifty miles south of Roanoke

239
00:07:20,887 --> 00:07:22,957
Archaeologists digging there have found English

240
00:07:22,957 --> 00:07:23,557
objects,

241
00:07:23,557 --> 00:07:25,557
like part of a sword handle and a writing

242
00:07:25,557 --> 00:07:26,612
slate

243
00:07:26,762 --> 00:07:28,392
They also found pieces of guns,

244
00:07:28,392 --> 00:07:30,472
and bits of metal and glass from the right

245
00:07:30,472 --> 00:07:31,408
time

246
00:07:31,558 --> 00:07:34,068
Some experts say these items could have arrived

247
00:07:34,068 --> 00:07:34,468
later,

248
00:07:34,468 --> 00:07:35,715
through trade

249
00:07:35,865 --> 00:07:37,919
Others believe the colonists slowly joined the

250
00:07:37,919 --> 00:07:38,935
Croatoan people,

251
00:07:38,935 --> 00:07:41,254
and became part of their community

252
00:07:41,404 --> 00:07:42,474
But years afterwards,

253
00:07:42,474 --> 00:07:44,754
people told stories of grey-eyed islanders who

254
00:07:44,754 --> 00:07:46,559
could read from books

255
00:07:46,709 --> 00:07:47,219
If so,

256
00:07:47,219 --> 00:07:49,386
their descendants may still live in the area

257
00:07:49,386 --> 00:07:50,506
today

258
00:07:54,050 --> 00:07:55,240
In 2012,

259
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:57,760
researchers took a closer look at a map John

260
00:07:57,760 --> 00:07:58,640
White had drawn,

261
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:00,774
kept at the British Museum

262
00:08:00,924 --> 00:08:02,874
The map was called La Virginea Pars,

263
00:08:02,874 --> 00:08:05,383
and it was painted by White himself

264
00:08:05,533 --> 00:08:06,963
Under a small paper patch,

265
00:08:06,963 --> 00:08:08,363
they found a hidden symbol:

266
00:08:08,363 --> 00:08:08,963
a fort,

267
00:08:08,963 --> 00:08:11,363
drawn about fifty miles inland

268
00:08:11,525 --> 00:08:13,875
Scientists used light and special scans to see

269
00:08:13,875 --> 00:08:15,427
what lay underneath

270
00:08:15,577 --> 00:08:17,367
Archaeologists dug at that spot,

271
00:08:17,367 --> 00:08:19,407
and found pieces of English pottery from the

272
00:08:19,407 --> 00:08:20,815
right period

273
00:08:20,965 --> 00:08:22,795
The spot was near where two rivers meet,

274
00:08:22,795 --> 00:08:25,395
at the western end of Albemarle Sound

275
00:08:25,656 --> 00:08:27,677
They called it Site X

276
00:08:27,827 --> 00:08:29,537
Some of the pottery was a type made in

277
00:08:29,537 --> 00:08:29,977
England,

278
00:08:29,977 --> 00:08:31,602
called Border ware

279
00:08:31,752 --> 00:08:33,302
Maybe the colonists split up,

280
00:08:33,302 --> 00:08:34,422
with some going south,

281
00:08:34,422 --> 00:08:36,420
and others going inland

282
00:08:36,570 --> 00:08:38,600
But some experts say the pottery could have

283
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:40,680
come from later settlers

284
00:08:44,083 --> 00:08:46,511
Not every theory has a happy ending

285
00:08:46,661 --> 00:08:48,531
Scientists studied the rings of very old

286
00:08:48,531 --> 00:08:50,529
cypress trees in the area

287
00:08:50,679 --> 00:08:52,549
Tree rings show that the colonists arrived

288
00:08:52,549 --> 00:08:54,469
during the worst drought in eight hundred

289
00:08:54,469 --> 00:08:55,475
years

290
00:08:55,625 --> 00:08:57,575
Even the local people struggled to find enough

291
00:08:57,575 --> 00:08:58,599
food

292
00:08:58,749 --> 00:08:59,539
Without crops,

293
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:01,859
starvation and disease may have taken many of

294
00:09:01,859 --> 00:09:02,744
them

295
00:09:02,894 --> 00:09:06,284
When the English founded Jamestown in 1607,

296
00:09:06,284 --> 00:09:08,884
they heard rumors about the lost colonists

297
00:09:09,419 --> 00:09:10,729
Others think they were attacked,

298
00:09:10,729 --> 00:09:12,329
perhaps by Spanish soldiers,

299
00:09:12,329 --> 00:09:14,401
or by enemies on the mainland

300
00:09:14,551 --> 00:09:16,501
One report claimed some of them had been living

301
00:09:16,501 --> 00:09:18,101
with another people further north,

302
00:09:18,101 --> 00:09:19,905
and were later attacked

303
00:09:20,055 --> 00:09:21,205
And some famous clues,

304
00:09:21,205 --> 00:09:24,085
like carved stones found in the 1930s,

305
00:09:24,085 --> 00:09:26,383
are now believed to be fakes

306
00:09:26,533 --> 00:09:28,003
Dozens of these stones turned up,

307
00:09:28,003 --> 00:09:30,003
telling a story that seemed too good to be

308
00:09:30,003 --> 00:09:31,123
true

309
00:09:34,550 --> 00:09:36,100
More than four hundred years later,

310
00:09:36,100 --> 00:09:38,476
the mystery is still unsolved

311
00:09:38,626 --> 00:09:41,096
Roanoke Island is now home to the Fort Raleigh

312
00:09:41,096 --> 00:09:42,856
National Historic Site

313
00:09:43,142 --> 00:09:43,612
Every year,

314
00:09:43,612 --> 00:09:45,092
archaeologists dig,

315
00:09:45,092 --> 00:09:46,894
looking for new clues

316
00:09:47,044 --> 00:09:49,554
Almost every summer since 1937,

317
00:09:49,554 --> 00:09:52,034
a play about the Lost Colony has been performed

318
00:09:52,034 --> 00:09:53,419
on the island

319
00:09:53,569 --> 00:09:55,519
Some hope that DNA could one day connect

320
00:09:55,519 --> 00:09:58,119
families living today to the lost colonists

321
00:09:58,759 --> 00:10:00,549
The nearby town is named Manteo,

322
00:10:00,549 --> 00:10:02,917
after the colonists' loyal friend

323
00:10:03,067 --> 00:10:03,657
Until then,

324
00:10:03,657 --> 00:10:05,897
nobody knows what happened to the people of

325
00:10:05,897 --> 00:10:07,017
Roanoke

326
00:10:07,236 --> 00:10:08,426
And the county is named Dare,

327
00:10:08,426 --> 00:10:10,720
after the little girl who vanished

328
00:10:10,870 --> 00:10:11,820
Or to Virginia Dare,

329
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:14,420
the first English child born in America

330
00:10:14,879 --> 00:10:15,709
Perhaps one day,

331
00:10:15,709 --> 00:10:17,789
the next clue will be found in the ground,

332
00:10:17,789 --> 00:10:19,869
or in our DNA

333
00:10:20,517 --> 00:10:22,147
One hundred and fifteen people

334
00:10:22,147 --> 00:10:23,187
One carved word

335
00:10:23,187 --> 00:10:24,397
No answer

336
00:10:24,547 --> 00:10:25,577
Was it Croatoan,

337
00:10:25,577 --> 00:10:26,577
a hidden fort,

338
00:10:26,577 --> 00:10:28,117
or something darker?

339
00:10:28,267 --> 00:10:30,591
What do you think happened to the Lost Colony?

340
00:10:30,741 --> 00:10:32,252
Tell me in the comments

341
00:10:32,402 --> 00:10:35,002
Subscribe so you don't miss the next episode
